From 5d94d0cdc6c4280be5c7c7169331bbd9dd6812d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:10:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: santabarbara: populate the FRU EEPROMs

Back 11 of the 18 FRU EEPROMs with images read from hardware, so guest
firmware can identify the MB, SCM, BSM, SWB, FIO, OCP NIC, E1.S
backplane and the four Rainbow modules instead of finding them blank.
The two board-id EEPROMs were erased on the sampled chassis, and the
second SCM EEPROM and the Rainbow submodule FRUs did not enumerate, so
those stay blank.

Each Rainbow module carries its own FRU, so the shared initialiser now
takes the image to install.

The content is sanitized: part and serial numbers masked, dates fixed,
asset tags replaced, distinct originals kept distinct. The OCP NIC
carries an OEM MultiRecord whose contents are undocumented; the record
is kept and its body zeroed.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
---
 hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_santabarbara.c | 456 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 443 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

